<p>In the latest development, U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Washington expects the war involving Iran to last &quot;weeks, not months,&quot; and that the United States can meet its goals without sending ground troops into combat. Rubio spoke after meeting G7 counterparts in France, as Israel and Iran continued to exchange strikes and the wider Gulf region stayed on alert. Rubio also said some U.S. forces are still deploying to the region to give President Trump &quot;maximum optionality&quot; if conditions change, even as Washington publicly says it sees a path to wrap up operations on a limited timeline. At the same time, President Trump said there have been &quot;productive negotiations&quot; toward a diplomatic outcome, while Rubio said the U.S. is waiting for a formal Iranian response to a 15-point proposal. Iran, however, says it has already rejected that proposal.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/p69DKuJ9eBrOEmHmoo1O2RdgA_k4dYg3-g2_A-z7tLkxdnPsksYsOpTVGwpWWJyit2DnB0vPPOddq004iDfvl0HTFWnG_ec47bSX1hFOUB_V0B09cAiq4UwPMT0svxkFzBMewGmhC69pLrxOGPODzUbzOA3FLm-wCzXOCr2b84gw8wyzv_kPuE8dZLDwNFb_u8Rm3y28dTRzlyYj4yvh0nR8aTODn3wimJhZA5wrOdL0Z7qf8ocrYBbLf39KjY1YQg0aS3ez9WxeSLrhcg' alt='US Secretary of State Marco Rubio speaks to the press after a G7 Foreign Ministers&#x27; meeting near Paris on March 27, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Ground-war concern: U.S. reinforcements have raised fears that an air campaign could expand into a longer ground conflict, even though Rubio said that is not the stated plan.</li><li>Regional spillover: A U.S. official told Reuters that an Iranian attack on an air base in Saudi Arabia wounded 12 U.S. military personnel, including two seriously, showing that the conflict has spread beyond Iran and Israel.</li><li>Energy disruption: The air war has already disrupted global energy supplies, raising concern that a longer escalation could add more pressure to oil and shipping markets.</li><li>Operational tempo: Rubio said the campaign was &quot;on or ahead of schedule,&quot; signaling Washington&#x27;s view that military operations are moving quickly against its stated timeline.</li></ul><blockquote>On or ahead of schedule in that operation, and expect to conclude it at the appropriate time here — a matter of weeks, not months. - Marco Rubio</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United States: Rubio said the operation was &quot;on or ahead of schedule,&quot; reflecting Washington&#x27;s view that it can meet its objectives on a limited timeline without shifting to a declared ground war. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1985991/rubio-says-war-on-iran-to-last-weeks-not-months-no-us-ground-troops-needed'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>President Trump: Trump extended a deadline by 10 days while also calling the contacts &quot;productive negotiations,&quot; suggesting the White House is still pairing military pressure with room for diplomacy. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1985991/rubio-says-war-on-iran-to-last-weeks-not-months-no-us-ground-troops-needed'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Iran: Tehran said no negotiations had begun and that it had already rejected the 15-point U.S. proposal, underscoring how wide the diplomatic gap remains. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1985991/rubio-says-war-on-iran-to-last-weeks-not-months-no-us-ground-troops-needed'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Israel: Israel said it was striking Tehran while also defending against missiles fired from Iran, reflecting its view that active military operations remain necessary. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/rubio-sees-us-action-iran-completed-weeks-airstrikes-rumble'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1985991/rubio-says-war-on-iran-to-last-weeks-not-months-no-us-ground-troops-needed'>Rubio says war on Iran to last ‘weeks not months’, no US ground troops needed</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-marco-rubio-iran-war-weeks-mo